claygo extension: child wrap (Clay_LayoutConfig.wrapChildren).

Applied on top of the verbatim upstream clay.h by oracle/Makefile to build
clay_ext.h. This patch carries only what has to live inside upstream's own
structs and functions: the wrapChildren and wrapLineGap config fields, the
Clay__WrapLine type, the element and context fields, one-line hooks tagged
"claygo extension: child wrap", and one #include of patches/child-wrap.h,
which holds the extension's functions as plain C.

Never edit the hunks in place. `make rebase-patch` applies this patch onto
clay.h as clay_ext.h.work; edit that file, then `make refresh-patch` re-diffs
it with current line numbers and context. See oracle/UPSTREAM.md
("Extensions") and docs/child-wrap-spec.md.

